<title>UK: EIB sets 1.0 trillion lire-into-euro Eurobond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 1.0 trillion lire-into-euro Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank has launched a 1.0 trillion lire Eurobond due February 2007 which will carry a 9.00 percent coupon until February 1999, joint lead managers Banca Nazionale del Lavoro, Credito Italiano and Paribas said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The coupon will step down to 5.75 percent from February 1999. The deal is redenominatable into euros after EMU.  </p>
<p>The coupon step-down is unconditional.</p>
